      "message": "It seems a bit of a shame that lookup(), which feels like it should be a read operation, and might be quite common, needs a write lock.\n\nLooking at the code, it seems like the only reason for that is that we might have to increment an InodeState\u0027s handle_ref_count.\n\nIf we made that an atomic instead of a raw u64, then you wouldn\u0027t need \u0026mut to be able to increment it (but the increment would be marginally more expensive).\n\nDoes that seem like it might be a good tradeoff?",
